<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Publius Sittius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/44-bce">44 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Publius Sittius was a Roman adventurer from Nuceria who led a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. During Caesar's African campaign in 46 BCE he invaded Numidia with King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bocchus-ii">Bocchus II</a> of Mauretania and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirta">Cirta</a>, forcing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-i">Juba I</a> to divide his forces. Caesar rewarded him with the lands around Cirta, which he settled with his followers, and he was killed in 44 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/publius-sittius.jpg" alt="Publius Sittius" width="320" height="149" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Publius_Sittius.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
